<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korean corporate bond issues to rise in February.</title>
<headline>S.Korean corporate bond issues to rise in February.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The government-controlled Korea Securities Dealers Association said on Friday it has approved plans for 2.6 trillion won in new corporate bond issues in February.</p>
<p>The approved amount was an increase from 2.3 trillion won worth of new corporate bonds issued in January, a statement from the association said.</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5643</p>
</text>
